1
00:00:01,751 --> 00:00:05,463
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:09,342
<i>Billy.</i>

3
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:12,512
<i>Uh… What are you doing here?</i>

4
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:16,725
<i>You said you wanted to</i>
<i>prove yourself, right?</i>

5
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,060
<i>What can I do? How can I help?</i>

6
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,311
<i>Chief.</i>

7
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:23,106
<i>Bea is here.</i>

8
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:25,442
<i>I asked her to come here.</i>

9
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:28,903
<i>I have a favor to ask from all of you.</i>

10
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>And I need your cooperation on this.</i>

11
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:35,493
<i>So, Bea and I will stage a fight.</i>

12
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:39,122
<i>It needs to be convincing.</i>

13
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>I just want to help.</i>

14
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,668
<i>I'll do anything. Just tell me.</i>

15
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:46,171
<i>Wow!</i>

16
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,840
<i>Let's give this liar a round of applause!</i>

17
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:49,924
[APPLAUSE]

18
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,634
<i>Great acting!</i>

19
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>You're crossing the line.</i>

20
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:57,932
<i>Don't act like you never did</i>
<i>anything wrong in your life.</i>

21
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:00,435
<i>I wanted to change and help,</i>
<i>but you refused.</i>

22
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:04,397
<i>You'd rather I stay evil?</i>
<i>Well, all right, then.</i>

23
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:06,733
<i>I'll give you what you want.</i>

24
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:09,694
<i>And I'll make sure you regret it, Billy.</i>

25
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:11,613
[KAREN] <i>Wow.</i>

26
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>So it's true that Billy</i>
<i>really despises you.</i>

27
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:17,410
<i>She does. She made me and my mom suffer.</i>

28
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,704
<i>That's why my mom is in prison right now.</i>

29
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:23,124
<i>But now, it turns out that</i>
<i>she's also a criminal.</i>

30
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:27,462
<i>Good thing I found you.</i>

31
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:28,588
<i>Now I have allies.</i>

32
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:31,216
<i>We're on the same side, but remember,</i>

33
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:33,343
<i>we're only allies up to Plan B.</i>

34
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:35,845
<i>I'll send her a video and post it</i>

35
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:37,722
<i>if she doesn't hold up</i>
<i>her end of the deal.</i>

36
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:40,600
<i>But since I like to play it safe…</i>

37
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:42,936
<i>Fine, I'll go along with your plan.</i>

38
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:44,854
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

39
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,815
[KAREN] <i>Jordan was at our house.</i>

40
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:47,857
[DINO] <i>Huh?</i>

41
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>How did he find out where we live?</i>

42
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,402
<i>- Is it true?</i>
<i>- What do you mean?</i>

43
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,988
<i>He believes that you're the one</i>
<i>who killed his mother.</i>

44
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:56,658
<i>Well? Is it true?</i>

45
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:58,910
<i>You killed your wife.</i>

46
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:00,286
<i>Just admit it!</i>

47
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:02,080
<i>Tell me!</i>

48
00:02:02,747 --> 00:02:05,458
<i>Speak up! You killed Jade!</i>

49
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:08,336
<i>You did, right? So you did kill her!</i>

50
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:10,171
<i>- She pushed my patience!</i>
<i>- Huh?</i>

51
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,714
<i>I had no other choice!</i>

52
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,092
<i>Everything that happened</i>
<i>that day was Jade's fault.</i>

53
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:15,927
<i>It was all her fault!</i>

54
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,518
<i>Make way, please!</i>

55
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:25,311
<i>- What happened?</i>
<i>- Move back, please.</i>

56
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:32,902
<i>Publicity stunt? Really?</i>

57
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,530
<i>A wanted fugitive</i>
<i>was caught, guys.</i>

58
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:38,408
<i>He blackmailed Billy</i>
<i>and killed Jordan's mother.</i>

59
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:41,411
<i>That's not a marketing campaign.</i>
<i>That's a crime.</i>

60
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,580
<i>And she helped bring justice.</i>

61
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:46,875
<i>I doubt a CEO would get herself</i>
<i>involved in a murder case</i>

62
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,418
<i>just for clout.</i>

63
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,962
<i>Wake up, haters. Use your brains.</i>

64
00:02:55,717 --> 00:03:01,806
[PENSIVE MUSIC
PLAYING]

65
00:03:03,766 --> 00:03:05,268
FUGITIVE DINO VALENTIN ARRESTED

66
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:08,187
EVERYTHING'S JUST A PUBLICITY STUNT.

67
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:12,901
[PENSIVE MUSIC
CONTINUES]

68
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:24,954
THIS CLOUT CHASER
IS SO DESPERATE TO TREND!

69
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:30,585
CAN'T THEY JUST SHUT UP FOR ONCE?
ALWAYS STIRRING UP SOMETHING!

70
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:40,929
[DOOR OPENS]

71
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,142
- Dude.
- [BILLY] Yes?

72
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,560
Let's go. Everyone's waiting.

73
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,396
Okay.

74
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:08,414
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:01,676
[BLAIRE] Chief!

76
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:04,220
I'm so excited about this!

77
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,639
- [BLAIRE EXCLAIMS]
- Girl, calm down.

78
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:09,142
We're all excited here, Blaire.

79
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:11,019
So, I think we can start?

80
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,186
Okay. Charm?

81
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,063
Okay.

82
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:16,482
So, Billy and I discussed it,

83
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:19,152
and after everything that's happened,

84
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:22,322
we agreed that we need a fresh start.

85
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:25,116
We reviewed where we are today

86
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:27,076
and where we wanted to be.

87
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,495
So, first things first,

88
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,081
we're not changing our name.

89
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,334
We're still LoveList.

90
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,877
- [SLAMS ON TABLE]
- Yay!

91
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,254
- [BLAIRE CLAPS]
- [LAUGHTER]

92
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:43,051
Have a drink first.
You're like a little kid.

93
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:45,094
So, chief, what are we rebranding?

94
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:49,807
So, we're redefining what LoveList means.

95
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:54,228
Before, we helped our users
find "the right one."

96
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:58,066
Now, I want LoveList to be with our users,

97
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,317
not just at the start,

98
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,986
but through every stage
of their love lives.

99
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:06,991
Whether healing from a heartbreak,

100
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:09,786
finding the courage to date again,

101
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:13,664
finding the one, and learning to build

102
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:16,292
a healthy relationship with a loved one,

103
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,962
LoveList is your companion.

104
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:27,804
We've all been through so much.

105
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,056
You all know that.

106
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:32,058
Yes.

107
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:34,936
We've stumbled, faced challenges,

108
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:37,897
and gotten back up time and again.

109
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:42,527
And maybe that's exactly
what our users need to see.

110
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:45,530
That love isn't about perfection.

111
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:48,366
It's about choosing to stay.

112
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:50,618
[BLAIRE CLAPS]

113
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:54,997
So, speaking of a fresh start,

114
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:59,710
here's our first direction
for the new visual identity.

115
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:03,631
<i>The app shouldn't stop working</i>
<i>once two people meet.</i>

116
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:06,551
<i>That's when people actually need us.</i>

117
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,302
You're right, Toni.

118
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:11,556
We will introduce
journey-based experiences.

119
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:15,309
So, if the user is recovering
from a heartbreak,

120
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,478
they'll see different content

121
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:20,815
compared to a user
who's just starting to go on dates.

122
00:07:20,898 --> 00:07:24,485
Now, if they are already
in a relationship,

123
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,195
we will help them nurture it.

124
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,655
Now, once they log in,

125
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:31,409
what we need to do is
find out what they need.

126
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:32,452
Okay?

127
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,580
Okay, so,

128
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,124
"Where are you in your love journey?"

129
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:40,209
"Healing after a heartbreak?"

130
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:42,003
"Ready to meet someone?"

131
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:44,547
"Situationship or dating?"

132
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:46,799
"Building a serious relationship?"

133
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:50,845
And here's what we can offer them.

134
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:58,019
Matchmaking, daily tips,
relationship check-ins,

135
00:07:58,102 --> 00:08:01,439
expert advice, and a love tracker.

136
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:04,484
A companion.

137
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,110
Not just a matchmaker.

138
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:11,199
[BLAIRE CLAPPING]
Oh, so that's it!

139
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:15,870
So, we're not just helping people
find love anymore.

140
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:18,915
We're staying with them
while they figure it out.

141
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:20,291
Mm-hmm.

142
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:23,127
So, for the lonely hearts,

143
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:26,464
the healing hearts,
and the hopeful hearts.

144
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,382
- Aw.
- Right.

145
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:31,427
LoveList becomes that someone

146
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:34,889
who reminds people that they're not alone.

147
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,349
[BLAIRE] Yes.

148
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:37,934
Like a best friend.

149
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:39,435
[MORRIE] Mmm!

150
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:43,606
"LoveList, your best friend in love."

151
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:44,690
[MORRIE] Hmm?

152
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:47,735
"Your best friend in love."

153
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:50,112
- [BLAIRE GASPS, SOBS]
- [MORRIE] Mm-hmm.

154
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,573
That's beautiful!

155
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:53,741
- Right?
- Yeah.

156
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,660
[BLAIRE] I want a best friend too.

157
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:58,371
Why don't you make me
your best friend? BFF!

158
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:01,123
- Take me as your best friend!
- How about Morrie?

159
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:02,833
- Just stick with Morrie.
- Stick with him.

160
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:04,210
He's already my best friend,

161
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:07,129
but I don't think he can
help me with love.

162
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:12,343
How's life treating you, Ma?

163
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,470
Are you eating well here?

164
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,847
Don't worry about me.

165
00:09:17,765 --> 00:09:19,392
Are you sure everything's fine, Mariela?

166
00:09:22,478 --> 00:09:28,901
I just want to apologize again for what
I did to your daughter and Precious.

167
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:30,653
Mariela.

168
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:38,411
I'll apologize to you over and over.

169
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:41,539
Remember that.

170
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:46,335
It's enough for me
that both of you are on good terms now.

171
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:49,672
Take care of each other, okay?

172
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:52,967
And you? Are you doing well?

173
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:55,636
I'm doing great, Ma.

174
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:58,556
Billy helped me out
with some startup capital,

175
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:01,934
and now we're business partners
in an internet cafe.

176
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:03,394
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

177
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:05,104
Not only that.

178
00:10:05,187 --> 00:10:09,900
I'm also working part-time at LoveList.

179
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:12,945
You see, I'm really trying to save money

180
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:15,364
because I want to buy
a small piece of land

181
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:17,700
and build a modest house on it.

182
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:22,455
That way, when you're released,
we can all live there together.

183
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:25,082
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,709
Uh…

185
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:30,713
Your father has a different life now.

186
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,465
Yeah, that's true.

187
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,302
- Of course.
- We have to accept that.

188
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:37,678
- Mm-hmm.
- Dear.

189
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:40,598
From now on,

190
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:46,103
I'm dedicating my life to making amends
to all of you whom I've hurt.

191
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:48,814
The same goes for me, Pa.

192
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:54,403
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:57,365
Ma?

194
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,743
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- [BEA GIGGLES]

195
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:01,994
Come over here, Ma.

196
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:03,913
[ENRICO, MARIELA CHUCKLE]

197
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:07,708
- [MARIELA AND BEA SIGH HAPPILY]
- [ENRICO BREATHES DEEPLY]

198
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,128
[SIGHING]

199
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,969
Yes, I understand, LoveLister Joanne.

200
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:22,098
Healing takes time.

201
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,017
Forgiveness isn't instant,

202
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:29,730
even if you've accepted the apology
of the person who hurt you.

203
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:34,735
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,455
If you're still hurt,

205
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:49,375
or if every now and then,

206
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:53,379
you're still affected
by the history of betrayal,

207
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:58,092
if you can't help but question
that person's sincerity,

208
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:02,430
I'm telling you, that's normal.

209
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:07,184
But it doesn't make you
a bad person, okay?

210
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:11,397
It just means that the healing

211
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:14,275
is still happening.

212
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:18,279
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

213
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:21,490
Healing should never be rushed.

214
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:24,285
As they say,

215
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,913
there's nothing you can do
to change the past.

216
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,502
But here's the good news.

217
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:36,464
Look around you.

218
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:42,595
There are many people
who stand by you, support you,

219
00:12:42,678 --> 00:12:44,638
on the road to recovery.

220
00:12:44,722 --> 00:12:46,182
And eventually,

221
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:48,851
forgiveness.

222
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:54,732
[MUSIC TURNS BRIGHT]

223
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:04,742
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

224
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:13,834
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:19,924
[BEA]<i> I have wronged you</i>
<i>in so many ways.</i>

226
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:26,430
<i>I used the anger that filled my heart</i>

227
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:30,726
<i>and manipulated you to do my bidding.</i>

228
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:34,104
<i>In the end,</i>

229
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:38,234
<i>I led you here.</i>

230
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:41,654
<i>I hope you can forgive me, Caloy.</i>

231
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:44,740
<i>To this day,</i>

232
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:47,535
<i>I regret it.</i>

233
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:53,082
<i>I don't know if I can ever forgive myself.</i>

234
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,585
[SNIFFLES]

235
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,754
<i>But there's one thing I'm sure of.</i>

236
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:05,052
<i>You will forever remain in my heart.</i>

237
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:10,891
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:14:11,642 --> 00:14:13,519
[OLIVER] Come on!

239
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:17,398
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

240
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:18,482
[OLIVER] Hurry!

241
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:20,818
Oh no, talk about bad timing.

242
00:14:20,901 --> 00:14:22,653
You should stay longer. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

243
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,239
Is everything okay here?

244
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:26,740
- Yes, ma'am.
- Good.

245
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,327
Well, are you winning now?

246
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:31,871
- Yes, Bea.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

247
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:34,748
[BEA] What?

248
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:35,916
Oh!

249
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,419
Your time's almost up.

250
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:41,422
Well, Papa isn't here yet.

251
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:42,840
Extend, please?

252
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:44,884
[BEA] Extend? By how many minutes?

253
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,803
Hmm. Ten minutes?

254
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,681
- A ten-minute extension?
- Please?

255
00:14:50,764 --> 00:14:51,974
Hmm, I guess--

256
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:53,726
- [OLIVER] You love me, right?
- [BEA] Oh!

257
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:56,437
I was about to say yes,
but then Papa showed up.

258
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,188
- Pa, he's requesting ten more minutes.
- Pa…

259
00:14:58,272 --> 00:14:59,356
- Ten minutes?
- Please?

260
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,525
- Just ten?
- Haven't you been playing for a while now?

261
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,027
- Ten?
- I'm almost done.

262
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:03,986
I'll be quick.

263
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:06,238
Ten minutes for ten hugs.

264
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,908
- Deal? Okay.
- Throw in a kiss too.

265
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:10,826
- I love you! Mwah!
- Mwah! Mwah!

266
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,036
Okay. Ten minutes.

267
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:13,621
- Ten minutes, huh?
- Promise?

268
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,331
- [WHISPERS] Twelve minutes.
- [SQUEALS] Let's go!

269
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:16,498
Thank you, Bea! I love you!

270
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,416
Look at him, Pa.

271
00:15:17,499 --> 00:15:20,544
Auntie, I bet they'll be home soon.

272
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:21,712
Oh, they're finally here.

273
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:23,047
- Someone's happy.
- Hello!

274
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,633
- What's up?
- I'm a happy kid.

275
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:26,926
- Greet Auntie too.
- Oh.

276
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,636
- Hi, Pa.
- Okay, wait a minute.

277
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:30,679
- I'll just grab a plate.
- Bea.

278
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,848
- Everything looks good.
- Have dinner with us.

279
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:33,849
- Come on.
- Okay.

280
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:34,975
[OLIVER] Come, come, come!

281
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:36,602
- Bea, sit next to me.
- [CHAIR SCRAPING]

282
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,145
[PRECIOUS] Come on, join us for dinner.

283
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:41,774
We're ten minutes late because someone
wanted to play a little longer.

284
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,692
- Geez!
- [ENRICO, PRECIOUS CHUCKLE]

285
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:46,612
Who was that stubborn someone?

286
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:48,197
- [BILLY] I'm wondering.
- [ENRICO] This looks delicious.

287
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,699
- I'll grab some food now.
- Sure, go ahead, Pa.

288
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:52,326
I'm starving.

289
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,787
Thank you, Pa.

290
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:55,704
Let me.

291
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:58,123
- Can Oliver have some?
- Just a little, Bea.

292
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,249
She said just a little.

293
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,627
- Don't forget the vegetables.
- Just about two scoops of rice.

294
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,003
Try your favorite fish too.

295
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:09,301
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

296
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:15,975
[ENRICO] Rice is life!

297
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:18,143
- Mmm.
- I'll eat just a little rice.

298
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,561
[PRECIOUS] The food is good.

299
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,313
[ENRICO] I'll have some of this too.

300
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,608
- Here you go, Auntie.
- Thank you.

301
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:27,820
- You shouldn't eat too much either.
- Thanks, Pa.

302
00:16:27,903 --> 00:16:29,238
Here, take this.

303
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:33,367
Bea, it's okay. Let me do that.
It's getting late.

304
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:36,036
Billy, come on. Just let me help you.

305
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,413
I want to help.

306
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,916
- Okay--
- Oh. Billy, hang on.

307
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,337
Billy.

308
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:48,340
For you.

309
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:51,135
I bought these with my first paycheck,

310
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:54,179
from our very first earnings
from the internet cafe.

311
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:56,473
- Mmm.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

312
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:59,143
- Congrats.
- Thanks.

313
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,436
It's all thanks to you.

314
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:05,274
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:17:22,916 --> 00:17:23,917
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

316
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:26,920
[CHUCKLING]

317
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,759
- Wow!
- Mm-hmm.

318
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:33,927
It's just replacement for the red shoes.

319
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:34,970
[BILLY] Thank you.

320
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,014
Thank you, my sister.

321
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:38,766
Finally.

322
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:41,852
Let's wash the dishes now.

323
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:42,978
Wait.

324
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:47,399
[PLATES CLATTERING]

325
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:55,157
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

326
00:17:58,243 --> 00:17:59,995
[MUSIC FADES]

327
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:02,122
After everything we've been through,

328
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:05,793
I'm happy that
we're all still together to this day.

329
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:08,212
We're persevering and we're complete.

330
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:13,801
So, I hope that you'll also
learn to forgive yourself.

331
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,720
I can't do that without you.

332
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:20,474
By the way, Mariela asked me
to apologize to you on her behalf.

333
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:24,561
She also said that
she's no longer opposed…

334
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:27,397
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] To our relationship?

335
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:29,733
Precious…

336
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:33,529
My love for you won't fade. You know that.

337
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,948
But I've made too many mistakes.

338
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:38,283
I'll do my best to make up for it.

339
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:42,121
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

340
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:46,667
But I have to take care
of my children first.

341
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,131
I hope you understand.

342
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,424
Of course I do.

343
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:56,802
Everything you've said is right.

344
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:59,555
You should prioritize your children first.

345
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:01,682
You should focus on that first.

346
00:19:03,725 --> 00:19:04,893
Thank you.

347
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,481
- [BILLY] Got everything?
- [BEA] Mm-hmm.

348
00:19:09,565 --> 00:19:12,901
Oliver? They're leaving!

349
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:16,905
- Dad, I packed you some food.
- [ENRICO] Mm!

350
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:18,115
[BEA] That'll be mine instead.

351
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:19,741
[ENRICO] Right,
she'll finish it up herself.

352
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:21,535
- Oh, she'll eat it all.
- Mm.

353
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,828
Okay.

354
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:25,831
- [OLIVER] Bye-bye, Pa!
- [ENRICO] Bye-bye.

355
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:27,249
[OLIVER] Extension?

356
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,168
Extension? You've made us
extend a lot already.

357
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:30,210
- I know, right?
- [CHUCKLING]

358
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:31,795
- But, Bea…
- Mm?

359
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:34,840
I hope you and Papa
will visit us more often.

360
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:37,843
Of course! Won't I be the one
to take you home from the…

361
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:39,845
[OLIVER AND BEA]
Internet cafe!

362
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:41,847
- Bye-bye.
- Mm!

363
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:43,265
Okay.

364
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:53,650
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:56,904
<i>My grandson.</i>

366
00:19:56,987 --> 00:20:02,451
<i>T-Take me home.</i>

367
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,912
<i>Okay, Grandpa.</i>
[SNIFFLES]

368
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:15,297
<i>You know, I'm sure</i>
<i>they're both proud of you.</i>

369
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,342
<i>Mm! That's what they told me.</i>

370
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,303
<i>Look.</i>

371
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,681
<i>You got everything you wanted.</i>

372
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:26,600
<i>Not quite yet.</i>

373
00:20:31,688 --> 00:20:34,024
<i>When you love someone,</i>
<i>don't hide your feelings.</i>

374
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:36,360
<i>Don't wait another day to tell them.</i>

375
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,656
<i>Let the world know how you feel.</i>

376
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:44,576
<i>Love is like a canvas.</i>

377
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:49,122
<i>If you're scared to make</i>
<i>your first brushstroke</i>,

378
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:51,541
<i>you won't be able to create anything.</i>

379
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:57,506
<i>When you're sure about that person,</i>
<i>don't be afraid.</i>

380
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,007
<i>Go for it.</i>

381
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:04,179
<i>What if we upgrade</i>
<i>our features on LoveLine?</i>

382
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:07,891
<i>We could include counseling for couples.</i>

383
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:10,686
<i>Only if it's okay with you.</i>
<i>What do you think?</i>

384
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:14,481
<i>Hello?</i>

385
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:15,941
<i>I'll miss this.</i>

386
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,986
<i>There's nothing like this in Australia.</i>

387
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:21,154
<i>Huh?</i>
